From f6a8186b6ed820f4cd86e3616e5398549f02de86 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 09:50:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 20/22] feat(crypto): printable paper key with QR code

pbscommon: NewPaperKey renders a key file like `proxmox-backup-client key
paperkey`: the key file pretty-printed as serde_json does ("kdf": null
included) between the BEGIN/END markers, a QR code of it (EC level M,
via rsc.io/qr) and a standalone printable HTML page with escaped caller
text. ProtectKeyConfig wraps a key in a passphrase-protected key file
(scrypt, as `key create` does) for a copy that is useless without the
passphrase. ParseKeyConfig, and so LoadKeyConfig, also accept the text
copied off a paper key; the markers count only on a line of their own.
